{%- comment -%}
  Sticky buy bar. Fixed to the bottom of the viewport with safe-area inset for
  iPhone, and present at every width — the desktop buy box is sticky only for
  as long as the PDP's first section lasts, and past it there is no way to buy
  without scrolling back up.

  It appears once [data-buybar-anchor] leaves the screen and hides again over
  [data-buybar-hide]. On the product template the anchor is the buy box itself,
  so the bar arrives at exactly the moment the real Add to Cart scrolls away
  and never competes with it — the two are never on screen together. Elsewhere
  the anchor is the hero.

  No purchase logic of its own: the form carries [data-buybox-form], which is
  the same delegated handler the buy box and the product card submit through.
  Off the product page there is nothing to add, so it links to the product.

  What the bar owes the shopper is what they are buying, what it costs, and one
  way to act on it: thumbnail, name, price, CTA. The price is set compact and
  the name truncates to one line, so the row stays a single band rather than
  growing a second one on a long product title.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign p = product | default: settings.featured_product
  assign on_pdp = false
  if template.name == 'product'
    assign on_pdp = true
  endif
  assign v = p.selected_or_first_available_variant
-%}
{%- if p -%}
<div class="buybar" data-buybar role="region" aria-label="Quick purchase">
  <div class="buybar-media" aria-hidden="true">
    {%- if p.featured_image -%}
      {% render 'responsive-image',
         img: p.featured_image,
         alt: '',
         widths: '88,132',
         sizes: '44px',
         base_width: 88,
         loading: 'lazy' %}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Name over price, both in one column. The name is context and truncates to a
    single line; the price is the number being committed to and is the only
    thing in this stack carrying full ink. The CTA still outweighs both by an
    order of magnitude — it is solid, 48px and the only saturated object in the
    bar — which is what keeps a three-part row from turning into a toolbar.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="buybar-info">
    <p class="buybar-title">{{ p.title }}</p>
    {% render 'price', variant: v, compact: true %}
  </div>

  {%- if on_pdp -%}
    <form class="buybar-form" data-buybox-form>
      <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ v.id }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
      {%- comment -%}
        Same pending pattern as every other add-to-cart surface: both words
        ship and CSS shows one, keyed off the aria-busy the shared handler
        sets. Nothing spins and nothing animates.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <button type="submit" class="buybar-cta" data-add-to-cart {% unless v.available %}disabled{% endunless %}>
        {%- if v.available -%}
          <span class="btn-label">Add to Cart<span class="visually-hidden"> — {{ p.title }}</span></span>
          <span class="btn-pending" aria-hidden="true">Adding&hellip;</span>
        {%- else -%}Sold out{%- endif -%}
      </button>
    </form>
  {%- else -%}
    <a class="buybar-cta" href="{{ p.url }}">View product</a>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{ "name": "Sticky buy bar" }
{% endschema %}
